[{"id":4629188743,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABE-vQhw","user":{"login":"Akosmo","id":95504962,"node_id":"U_kgDOBbFKQg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/95504962?u=80438adc5ffbc7bbf00b64757b445f273cf333b2&v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo","html_url":"https://github.com/Akosmo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Makes sense to me. Here's how things currently work:\n- When `AudioStreamPlayer.play()` is called, the playback will be instantiated, and then started in the audio server, setting its state to `PLAYING`, thus allowing mixing to happen there.\n- When the scene tree is paused, it'll only pause relevant playbacks that are already playing. If tree is unpaused, all relevant existing playbacks will also unpause.\n\nThis means that if `AudioStreamPlayer.play()` is called while the scene tree is paused, playback will still start because the function doesn't check if the node can process. This is changed with this PR.\n\nNow what happens with this PR is:\n- After playback is instantiated and started in the audio server, `AudioStreamPlayer.play()` checks if the node can process. If it can't, `NOTIFICATION_PAUSED` is sent to `AudioStreamPlayerInternal.notification()`, which then pauses all playbacks, including the new one, setting its state in the audio server to `PAUSED`, disallowing mixing there.\n\nTested. Issue is valid and this PR fixes it to me.","state":"APPROVED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114764#pullrequestreview-4629188743","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/114764","author_association":"MEMBER","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114764#pullrequestreview-4629188743"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/114764"}},"submitted_at":"2026-07-04T08:29:10Z","commit_id":"b193c4beeb124d8796089d19f0d548ad05352037"},{"id":4882830296,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABIwoT2A","user":{"login":"Jaytheway","id":22476284,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNDc2Mjg0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22476284?u=02d933b530b26d757decb436944bf86bbcb046b2&v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jaytheway","html_url":"https://github.com/Jaytheway","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jaytheway/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jaytheway/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jaytheway/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jaytheway/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jaytheway/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jaytheway/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jaytheway/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jaytheway/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jaytheway/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**There are 2 potential problems:**\r\n\r\n1. It is very unlikely, but technically nothing ensures the new stream playback won't start mixing before the pause notification received. At the end of `AudioServer::start_playback_stream()`, the stream is handed off to the list processed by the audio thread concurrently, it may happen that the audio thread will start mixing the new playback node as soon as it's added to the list.\r\nIn such case it will mix one full block of audio from the new stream before the pause request reaches the playback node.\r\n\r\n2. Another problem is that sending pause notification triggers \"fade out to pause\" behavior\", it doesn't immediately stop the mixing. This means that even if the playback node hasn't started mixing yet (as described in the first issue), the playback will start shortly with `FADE_OUT_TO_PAUSE` state and will be mixed with a fade out. This could be an audible pop. Or in the best case scenario the beginning of the audio source has some silence, or is very quiet, which will mask this issue.\r\n\r\n--- \r\nPotential workaround could be to not start the playback, but save the state for the playback to start on `NOTIFICATION_UNPAUSED` from `AudioStreamPlayer`. ","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114764#pullrequestreview-4882830296","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/114764","author_association":"NONE","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114764#pullrequestreview-4882830296"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/114764"}},"submitted_at":"2026-08-07T12:31:03Z","commit_id":"b193c4beeb124d8796089d19f0d548ad05352037"},{"id":5177439696,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABNJl10A","user":{"login":"Jaytheway","id":22476284,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNDc2Mjg0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22476284?u=02d933b530b26d757decb436944bf86bbcb046b2&v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jaytheway","html_url":"https://github.com/Jaytheway","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jaytheway/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jaytheway/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jaytheway/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jaytheway/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jaytheway/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jaytheway/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jaytheway/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jaytheway/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jaytheway/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114764#pullrequestreview-5177439696","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/114764","author_association":"NONE","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114764#pullrequestreview-5177439696"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/114764"}},"submitted_at":"2026-09-11T10:04:46Z","commit_id":"dd342da3fe228ad1d1366dc596e12e97e2de6c6f"},{"id":5178291289,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABNKZ0WQ","user":{"login":"neclor","id":81529592,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxNTI5NTky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81529592?u=05540eca98e50671b0e0a42d273483169a80201c&v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/neclor","html_url":"https://github.com/neclor","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neclor/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neclor/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neclor/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neclor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neclor/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neclor/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neclor/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neclor/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neclor/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114764#pullrequestreview-5178291289","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/114764","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114764#pullrequestreview-5178291289"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/114764"}},"submitted_at":"2026-09-11T11:48:32Z","commit_id":"dd342da3fe228ad1d1366dc596e12e97e2de6c6f"},{"id":5530413364,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABSaNpNA","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?u=f7f8e0273f784f5ec6f6b7fe4a88d449896eb48a&v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Looks like it should work, but I don't like how this introduces new state via `deferred_plays`.\nWhen pausing while playing, the existing playbacks simply get paused. Using `deferred_plays` here is inconsistent and invites bugs.\n\nWhen playing while paused, I would expect the playbacks to get added as normal, just in a paused state to avoid an accidental initial mix call. That's currently not possible in the `AudioServer` API, but can trivially be added to `start_playback_stream`.","state":"CHANGES_REQUESTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114764#pullrequestreview-5530413364","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/114764","author_association":"MEMBER","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114764#pullrequestreview-5530413364"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/114764"}},"submitted_at":"2026-10-15T08:43:42Z","commit_id":"dd342da3fe228ad1d1366dc596e12e97e2de6c6f"}]